 "narrative": {
  "setting": "The Capitol Region holds 389,086 households in the 2023 survey, up from 386,549 a year earlier, and 994,115 residents, more than nearly all US counties and up 3.1% since 2020. Median household income of $93,394 exceeds that of about nine in ten counties, and 29.2% of households earn $150,000 or more. Growth is not coming from domestic moves, as net domestic migration was -105 in 2025.",
  "moving": "Recorded home sales fell from 12,157 in 2021 to 7,404 in 2023, recovered to 8,518 in 2024, and reached 6,378 through September 2025, so listing turnover is rebuilding but remains below its earlier level. The median sale price rose every year, from $246,000 in 2020 to $370,000 in 2025, and the median home value of $323,700 is up 28.6% since 2020. Permits for 1,146 homes in 2025 equal only 115.3 per 100,000 residents, below about two thirds of counties, and 714 sit in buildings of five or more units, adding little new for-sale stock.",
  "distress": "Foreclosure filings number 219 from July through September 2026 and 762 over the twelve months to September 30, 2026, with records held from April 21, 2025 to October 21, 2026. Collection began April 21, 2026, so earlier months include only cases still open that day and the twelve-month count understates actual volume. Probate filings number 39 in the three months and 447 over twelve, with records from December 27, 2024 to October 20, 2026, a steady source of inherited homes likely to be sold. Tax delinquency lists, liens and code enforcement cases are not held for this county.",
  "watch": "Probate filings of 39 in the latest quarter, against roughly 112 a quarter across the year, may reflect recording lag rather than a real decline. Net income migration of -305.5 per resident, below nearly nine in ten counties, indicates departing households carry more income than arriving ones. Sales of 8,518 in 2024 sit about 30% below 2021, and rising prices may narrow the buyer pool further.",
  "provide": "Red Planet Data already holds residential parcel records covering 274,406 parcels, owner records, home sales, foreclosure court filings and probate filings. No further record types are currently scheduled to be brought in, and tax delinquency lists, liens and code enforcement cases are not held or obtainable yet. The annual residential license price is $6,500 a year.",
